ny's short-sighted profit  motivated and anti-labor policies are  dooming Earth this also goes against the  balancing of energy that Navi follow on  Pandora they say the goddess airwa gives  energy for life but that it is only  borrowed and that you end up giving the  energy back in death however humans on  Earth presumably Rich humans are trying  to hoard their life and their energy and  not giving it back to Nature causing  disruption chaos and destruction on  their planet in the process  it's no secret that Avatar the way of  water director and co-redder James  Cameron is obsessed with the ocean he  spent tons of money from his own  personal Fortune to fund deep sea  Expeditions so it's no surprise that  some of that design aesthetic for the  rda's token hunting operations would  have some aesthetic similarities to real  ships and Subs even the more Fantastical  sci-fi designs such as the subs that  have metallic crab-like legs and  mechanical claws bare resemblances to  real Tech in the field of deep sea  diving James Cameron's love for the  ocean clearly extends to the various  Aquatic Life that inhabits it this  includes the whale-like Tolkien who live  in the ocean and visit the coastal  Villages of the marine-based mekayina  navi tribe nimakaina and Tolkien share a  close sacred Bond as the Tolkien  revealed to be sentient creatures  arguably smarter than both the humans  and Navi who are even capable of complex  language mathematics and even art at one  point Jake's younger son Loach befriends  a wounded and banished Tolkien  throughout the rest of the film Loach  and the banished Tolkien swim together  and grow a close and special bond  themselves the Tolkien even becomes  pivotal to the navi winning the final  battle against the large Tolkien hunting  ship this subplot seems to be similar to  the plot of the 1993 family film Free  Willy about a young boy who befriends a  mistreated Orca and then is able to free  it from captivity not only that but  there 